    "title": "Special Weather Statement by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-10 21:17:00 MDT Expires: 2025-09-10 22:00:00 MDT Urgency: Expected Severity: Moderate Certainty: Observed Instruction: Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening weather conditions. Target Area: Powder River; Carter At 917 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong thunderstorms extending from 17 miles east of Broadus to 22 miles west of Alzada, or extending from 17 miles east of Broadus to 38 miles southeast of Broadus, moving east at 30 mph.\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and pea size hail.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is possible.\nLocations impacted include... Alzada, Hammond, Boyes and Ridge.",
